            </pubStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_ff6e495b">
               <titlePage label="Title page" xml:id="titlePage_fdec437b">
                  <p xml:id="idm137">Johann Elias Schlegels | Werke, | Vierter Theil. | Herausgegeben | von | Johann Heinrich Schlegln, | Professor der Philosophie bey der Universität Kopenhagen, und | Secretär der königlich dänischen Kanzley. [emblem consisting of a lyre and a sceptre] | ___ | Kopenhagen und Leipzig, | In Verlage der Mummischen Buchhandlung. | 1766. </p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="Secondary title page (p. [203])" xml:id="titlePage_bf730fcb">
                  <p xml:id="idm139">Cantaten.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="Secondary title page (p. 217)" xml:id="titlePage_b010c70e">
                  <p xml:id="idm141">Cantaten. | ___ | Cantate. | Auf das Geburtsfest | der Kronprinzeß von Dänemark. | Den 18. December 1743. | ___ |</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_20250b2b">3 pages</extent>
               <watermark xml:id="watermark_5211f7e2">two partly visible watermarks on flyleaves, the first of which consist of the countermark or emblem 'J. Bassuet' with grapes above dating from the end of the eighteenth century or the beginning of the nineteenth century; the second flyleaf has 'M DANG <rend xml:id="idm144" rend="sup">MOIS</rend>' (cf. Gravell:5722).</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_119f0ad9">In 8<rend xml:id="idm146" rend="sup">o</rend>; front endpaper, front flyleaf, title page (sig. [*1r]), blank page (sig. [*1v]), foreword (sigs. *2r–*3v), table of contents (sig. *4r–v), text (pp. 3–320), end flyleaf, end endpaper; in all 320 pages. The relevant pages concerning the present cantata are pp. 217–19 and a foreword pp. [205]–06.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
